<title>GERMANY: GERMAN DATA DUE NEXT WEEK - Trade, GDP, jobless.</title>
<headline>GERMAN DATA DUE NEXT WEEK - Trade, GDP, jobless.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following German economic indicators are expected to be released next week:</p>
<p>    INDICATOR	PERIOD	 PREVIOUS		 EXPECTED</p>
<p>					    DATA		     DATE</p>
<p> Trade		 Sept	   +8.1 bln, c/a -4.6   Dec 3</p>
<p> GDP		   Q3	     +1.5 q/q, +1.2 y/y   Dec 4</p>
<p> Wholesale sales   Oct	    +0.7 m/m, -1.2 y/y   Dec 4 or 5</p>
<p> Unemployment	Nov	    4.040 million, 10.6 pct  Dec 5</p>
<p>NOTE - The Federal Statistics Office said the expected release dates were targets. Previous unemployment data show seasonally adjusted figures for October. The Economics Ministry is also expected to release data on industrial orders and production for October some time during the week.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
